{
 "_about": "Workflows (round 5, Settings > Workflows). Five starter workflows: two on (a partial payer offer needs a decision; follow-up call day) and three off (units running low; late notes; evidence gaps before a renewal), each valid and laid out on a 20 px grid. A workflow is blocks joined by links (web/js/shared/workflows/catalog.js); it only decides which bell items, suggestions and reminders a person sees. Nothing here sends, calls, files, signs or texts: every workflow carries the locked guardrail \"Nothing is sent, called or filed on its own\". Messages use only {patient} (initials), {payer} and {date}. The templates in web/js/shared/workflows/templates.js are these same graphs. workflow_confirmations lists a saved change that waits for a second person (two-person guardrail); empty at the start.",
 "workflows": [
